  "question": {
    "text": "The tangents at the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;on the parabola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;meet at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>. Then the area (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>unit</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>) of the triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is:",
